MAN: Oh, good morning. I''ve just moved into the area and I''d like to join the centre, if that''s still possible?
WOMAN: Of course. Let me take a few details and I''ll set up a membership record for you. Can I start with your full name?
MAN: Yes, it''s Daniel Whitcombe.
WOMAN: Could you spell the surname for me?
MAN: W-H-I-T-C-O-M-B-E.
WOMAN: Whitcombe, thank you. And your address?
MAN: It''s 42 Bramley Road. That''s B-R-A-M-L-E-Y.
WOMAN: Bramley Road, lovely. That''s the road behind the old station, isn''t it?
MAN: That''s the one, yes.
WOMAN: And a contact number?
MAN: My mobile is 0784 220 9163.
WOMAN: Let me read that back: 0784 220 9163.
MAN: Perfect.
WOMAN: Now, we offer three kinds of membership. There''s standard, which is thirty pounds a year; family, which is fifty; and concession, which is eighteen and is for students and people over sixty-five. Which would suit you?
MAN: I''m a full-time student, so the concession one, please.
WOMAN: Right, concession it is. I will need to see your student card when you come in, just the once. Now, which activities are you interested in? That helps us send you the right newsletter.
MAN: I''d really like to do something with swimming. Is the pool open in the mornings?
WOMAN: It is, from half past six. And there''s an adult swimming club on Tuesday evenings if you''d like something more structured.
MAN: I might, but let''s put swimming down for now.
WOMAN: Swimming, noted. And how did you hear about us? We ask everybody.
MAN: A neighbour mentioned it, actually. She swims here every week.
WOMAN: Lovely, I''ll put neighbour. Now, one last thing — is there anything we should know for safety reasons? Any medical condition?
MAN: I have asthma. It''s very well controlled, but I do carry an inhaler.
WOMAN: That''s useful for us to know, thank you. I''ll note asthma on your record. Your membership will start on the first of March, and your card will be ready to collect from the reception desk after that date. There''s a small charge for a replacement card, so do look after it.
MAN: Understood. Do I pay today?
WOMAN: You can pay when you collect the card. Oh, and do bring a padlock — the lockers in the changing rooms don''t have keys.
MAN: A padlock. Right, I''ll remember that.', ('2026-09-09 18:53:32'::timestamp AT TIME ZONE 'UTC')),
